      <workList xml:id="workDesc_b07f4141">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e230227">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_819abbaf">B2:036</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_15d18577" xml:lang="de">Cantate: In Festo Trinitatis</title>
            <title type="alternative" xml:id="title_f6f0903d" xml:lang="de">Wir haben einen Gott</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_ea3d4ed3">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_826e59b1">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <history xml:id="history_085eedb2">
               <p xml:id="idm186">The present church cantata is listed in the Breitkopf catalogue of 1761, suggesting that it originally belonged to the cantor <persName xml:id="idm187" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Carl Gotthelf Gerlach</persName> at Neukirche in Leipzig; it had been obtained by the publishers from Gerlach’s estate earlier that year. The surviving source, which consists of performance parts from around 1770, was most likely ordered from the catalogue. Later the master copy, which included both score and parts, was listed in the Breitkopf auction catalogue of 1836. The cantata might be an early work from the time before Scheibe was employed as Kapellmeister in Copenhagen.</p>
            </history>
